    <DataNode elementId="Man6GlcNAc2-protein-A123" textLabel="Man₆(GlcNAc)₂-[protein] (isomer 6A₁,₂,₃)" type="Metabolite">
      <Graphics centerX="645.7420654296875" centerY="320.811279296875" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="PMN, zhang, SRI, caspi">This is one of three isomers of Man&lt;sub&gt;6&lt;/sub&gt;GlcNAc&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt; chains that are found in &lt;i&gt;N&lt;/i&gt; glycans. The nomenclature used to identify high mannose glycans has not been standardized. Several earlier systems were insufficient to describe all possible isomers |CITS: [7954510][17719235][17685584]|. The nomenclature used here is that proposed by Prien et al |CITS: [19181540]|, which can represent all processing isomers. According to this nomenclature, the other two Man&lt;sub&gt;6&lt;/sub&gt;GlcNAc&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt; isomers are named |FRAME: Man6-GlcNAc2-protein-A12B2 &quot;isomer 6A&lt;sub&gt;1,2&lt;/sub&gt;B&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;&quot;| and |FRAME: Man6GlcNAc2-protein-A12B1 &quot;isomer 6A&lt;sub&gt;2,3&lt;/sub&gt;B&lt;sub&gt;1&lt;/sub&gt;&quot;|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="Man6GlcNAc2-protein-A123" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="an &amp;alpha;-D-Man-(1&amp;rarr;2)-&amp;alpha;-D-Man-(1&amp;rarr;3)-[&amp;alpha;-D-Man-(1&amp;rarr;2)-&amp;alpha;-D-Man-(1&amp;rarr;3)-[&amp;alpha;-D-Man-(1&amp;rarr;6)]-&amp;alpha;-D-Man-(1&amp;rarr;6)]-&amp;beta;-D-Man-(1&amp;rarr;4)-&amp;beta;-D-GlcNAc-(1&amp;rarr;4)-&amp;beta;-D-GlcNAc-1-L-asparaginyl-[protein]" />
